    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2KqTnUNu2fBCK6DFzU2qKbS)_\n\n## What\n`org-other-agenda` (yibie's board) hard-codes Tokyo Night hex colours in its 17 faces. They now come from the theme in use.\n\n- Seven accents (`urgent`, `crucial`, `focus`, `positive`, `calm`, `meek`, `mild`), each a list of theme faces: an `sp-*` semantic face first (coloured in the sp themes), then a standard face (`error`, `warning`, `link`, `success`, `shadow`, ...) so Lambda, Ef and Doric themes work too.\n- `sp-org-agenda-board-roles` says which accent each board face uses; `sp-org-agenda-board-accents` says what each accent is made of; `sp-org-agenda-board-block-mix` tints the time blocks.\n- Text faces inherit, so they follow theme changes. The active tab and time blocks need real colours and are recomputed on `sp-after-load-theme-hook`.\n- Docs: new section \"org-other-agenda colours\" in `docs/tangles/text/sp-org-agenda.org`, including \"Changing the accents\" (which variables to edit to reorder them). The `.el` is tangled from it. CHANGELOG entry under Themes.\n\n## Tested\nEmacs 29.3 batch, 6 ERT tests (`tests/sp-org-agenda-board-test.el`): the package's fixed colours are cleared, accents follow the semantic face and fall back to the standard one, reordering by role, tab and block backgrounds.\n\n## Not tested\nThe real board, the actual sp/Lambda/Ef/Doric themes, and how the colours look on screen.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiBzsj6UMvs8e9hUjd2)_",
